# M1 / B012 — caching, ci-cd, code-review.

C R167 OL WF-017 | MUST | CI pipelines reproduce the repository's supported build/test commands: inspect the repository first, add stages for the actual project rather than generic boilerplate, do not assume a database, Redis, Docker or frontend tooling, do not hardcode a database provider into a generic pipeline, do not make an unadopted formatter a mandatory gate, do not depend on developer-machine state and keep failures visible. | CI/CD pipelines | Enforced checks the project adopted.
C R168 OL DEP-018 | MUST NOT | Do not add Docker to a pipeline or project merely because it can be containerized; add container artifacts only when the project actually deploys containers. | CI/CD and containers | none stated
C R169 OL WF-019 | MUST | When deployment performs database migrations make the migration step explicit, use the project's approved credentials, run it at a controlled point and fail visibly; no automatic production seeding or startup migrations. | deployment pipelines | none stated
C R170 OL WF-011 | MUST | Code review identifies concrete defects and risks in the actual changed behavior, prioritized correctness, security/authorization, data integrity/persistence, architecture boundaries, concurrency/integration, missing meaningful tests, maintainability, credible performance; style preferences are not elevated above behavioral defects and code is not reported as a violation merely for differing from an unadopted pattern. | code review | none stated
C R171 OL WF-011 | MUST | Before judging conformance the review reads the changed code with enough surrounding code (callers, contracts, dependencies) and the owning rules and knowledge skills of every changed area; do not review isolated lines. | code review | none stated
C R172 OL GOV-003 | MUST NOT | Do not weaken required specified behavior or introduce unapproved product behavior: new length or numeric limits, reserved names or values, newly required fields, extra workflow restrictions, additional user-visible validation or newly chosen string-comparison semantics (including via database collation or framework defaults). | product behavior | Detail explicitly approved by the user with durable sources synchronized.
C R173 OL GOV-005 | DEFAULT | Internal implementation details that do not change observable product behavior are not product-behavior decisions and need no approval. | product behavior | none stated
C R174 OL WF-012 | MUST NOT | Do not manufacture review findings: no failures without a plausible execution path, no findings merely to populate categories, tool output is evidence rather than authority; when there are no meaningful findings say so and name important areas that could not be verified; no filler praise. | code review | none stated
C R175 OL WF-007 | MUST | Scope security and other deep checks by risk: use the full security-scan workflow only when the user requested a security audit, the change is materially security-sensitive or a concrete finding justifies broader investigation. | code review and verification | none stated
C R176 OL TST-009 | DEFAULT | For a bug fix with plausible recurrence expect a regression test unless equivalent coverage already exists; do not request duplicate tests. | tests for bug fixes | Equivalent coverage exists.
C X21 EX RUN-021,ARC-016 | MUST NOT (review defect) | Tracked persistence entities must not be cached across Unit of Work boundaries. | caching | none stated | RUN-021 governs invalidation consistency and ARC-016 the commit boundary; no oracle policy forbids caching tracked entities as such. | Caching EF-tracked entity instances in a cache shared across requests is a review defect.
C X22 EX WF-011,WF-012 | MUST | Code-review findings are reported ordered by severity, each with severity, file/location, what is wrong, why it matters and the smallest reasonable fix, using the fixed severity scale Critical / High / Medium / Low with defined meanings. | code review output | none stated | WF-011/WF-012 govern priorities and honesty of findings; the oracle does not prescribe a findings format or severity scale. | A review that lists issues without location, impact or severity does not follow the workflow.

